        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2f46c63d-ccfa-52df-bd4a-8c89c5da998e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Columbia River, Oregon, Washington, Palm Beach County, Florida, Tanner Creek\n- Projects: Cascade Locks and Canal, Oregon Portage Railroad\n- Landmarks: Lake Worth Lagoon, The Breakers, Royal Poinciana Hotel, Bonneville Dam\n- People: Henry Flagler\n\nFacts:\n- In 1894, Henry Flagler opened the Royal Poinciana Hotel beside Lake Worth Lagoon facing the inland waterway.\n- In 1896, the Cascade Locks and Canal was completed as a navigation project on the Columbia River between Oregon and Washington.\n- In the later years of the Oregon Portage Railroad's operation, the railroad ran from Tanner Creek to the Cascade Locks while the locks were still under construction.\n- Lake Worth Lagoon is located in Palm Beach County, Florida.\n- The Breakers occupies the beachfront portion of the former grounds of the Royal Poinciana Hotel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "07b0cb4b-3de1-55ef-912f-77955c09f85d",
        "text": "Page: Cascade Locks and Canal. Sentence: The Cascade Locks and Canal was a navigation project on the Columbia River between the U.S. states of Oregon and Washington, completed in 1896.\nPage: Lake Worth Lagoon. Sentence: The Lake Worth Lagoon is a lagoon located in Palm Beach County, Florida.\nPage: Oregon Portage Railroad. Sentence: It ran from Tanner Creek (near where Bonneville Dam was later built) to the Cascade Locks, which were under construction in the later years of the railroad's operation.\nPage: The Breakers (hotel). Sentence: It occupies the beachfront portion of the grounds of the Royal Poinciana Hotel, which Flagler had opened beside Lake Worth Lagoon facing the inland waterway in 1894.",
